-- title:
--   Powers of the weighted centre as intersections of translated powers
-- statement:
--   Arithmetic data. Let $q$ be a prime with $5 \le q$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, and $\xi \in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` provides a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\,\xi = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, and `hK` requires $K$ to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79): the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the rational $q$-expansion function field of the modular curve of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ attached to the subgroup `levelH (q*ℓ) M'`, i.e. the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   Throughout, for $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ the predicate [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) says of an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ that it implements the substitution attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ on $q$-expansions: for every weight $k$, every pair $f,g$ of modular forms for the level subgroup attached to `levelH (q*ℓ) M'` admitting integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ with $p_g$ having nonzero image, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is $p_f/p_g$, and every embedding $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\,\xi = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, the coefficientwise image of $\tau x$ under $\iota$, multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$, equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$.
--
--   Integral model. Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field, which is an $A$-algebra inside $L$ with $L$ as fraction field, and with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly; assume $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and that $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hξA`). Let $j \in K$ have underlying Laurent series the coefficient extension of the rational $j$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), with $j \ne 0$. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Here `chartAlgFin A K j` is the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the scheme obtained by glueing $\mathrm{Spec}$ of this algebra with $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the corresponding algebra for $j^{-1}$.
--
--   Supersingular point. Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of `chartAlgFin A K j` containing $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`), and assume `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin A K j` with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The Drinfeld-chart hypothesis `hArig` (seven conjuncts, summarised here) asserts: for every point $z$ of the two-chart model at which the image $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ in the stalk lies in the maximal ideal, and every point $y'$ of the chart $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin A K j` mapping to $z$ whose ideal satisfies the same supersingularity condition, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ carrying $\varpi$ to a generator of $\mathfrak{m}_W$, power series $f,u,v$ over $W$ in two variables with $u,v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v - fu\bigr)$, such that: $e$ carries constants from $A$ to $C(\sigma a)$; every level automorphism attached to some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserves `chartAlgFin A K j`; such an automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$ acts trivially modulo $y'$; every such automorphism acting trivially modulo $y'$ is induced by a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ fixing constants, acting on the variables by a matrix $M$ over $W$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$, with a scalar $c$ satisfying $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M \equiv c\gamma$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $c \equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; two primes of $S$ containing $\sigma\varpi$, not containing both variables, and with tangent directions $(a_1{:}b_1)$, $(a_2{:}b_2)$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$ satisfying $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ have distinct contractions to the stalk; for a prime with tangent direction $(1{:}0)$, an element of the chart algebra lies in the contraction of that prime exactly when all its Laurent coefficients lie in $\mathfrak{m}_A$; and the germ of [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) minus a suitable constant $a_0 \in A$ corresponds under $e$ to a power series $h$ lying in $(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ for some $e_0 \ge 1$ whose degree-$e_0$ form is nondegenerate in the stated sense.
--
--   Fixed local data. Let $z$, $\varpi_z$, $y'$ be as above (hypotheses `hϖz`, `hz`, `hy'`, `hss'`), with `hy'y` requiring $y'$ to correspond to $y$. Let $W_1$ be a complete discrete valuation ring, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), let $f_1,u_1,v_1$ be power series in two variables over $W_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1 \equiv$ [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W₁`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $= X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and let $e_1$ be a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1\bigr)$. The hypothesis `hW₁` (seven conjuncts, of the same shape as the conclusion of `hArig`, summarised above) requires this datum to have exactly those properties.
--
--   The weighted centre and the blow-up chart. Let $J$ be an ideal of `chartAlgFin A K j` and let `hJ` require $J$ to be the infimum of the set of ideals $J'$ for which there exist $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, a level automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving `chartAlgFin A K j`, and $J'$ the preimage under the restriction of $\tau$ of the contraction, along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$, of the ideal of $S$ generated by the images of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$; here $\mathrm{toC}$ is the map from the stalk to its adic completion and $\mathrm{germY}$ the canonical map from the chart algebra to the stalk at $z$ through the chart immersion. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ which `hB` requires to be the algebra generated over `chartAlgFin A K j` by $\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}$, scalars restricted to $A$. Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`).
--
--   Further hypotheses on $B$ and $W$. `hR1` (two clauses): `chartAlgFin A K j` $\le B$, and every element of $K$ is a quotient of elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator. `hR2` (three clauses): $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$, and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. `hR3` (five clauses): an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$; $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; an element of the chart algebra lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$; and $W$ is the set of fractions $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$. `hEQ` (five clauses): for any $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the elements of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, compatible with $A \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, and equivariant for level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$, through an element $c \in \mathrm{GF}(q^2)^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in the subgroup [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting by [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325), with $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserve $B$; every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ receives the centre of $B$ under some level automorphism attached to a $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; an element of $B$ all of whose translates under such automorphisms lie in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and a level automorphism attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ that preserves $y$ on the chart algebra preserves $W$.
--
--   Conclusion. With $\mathrm{STK}$ the stalk of the two-chart model at $z$, $\mathrm{CMP}$ its adic completion at the maximal ideal, $\mathrm{toC} : \mathrm{STK} \to \mathrm{CMP}$ the canonical map, $S$ and $\mathrm{mkS}$ as above, and $\mathrm{germY}$ the canonical map from `chartAlgFin A K j` to $\mathrm{STK}$, the assertion is: for every natural number $n$,
--   $$J^n = \inf\Bigl\{\,J' \;\Bigm|\; \exists\,\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M'),\ \exists\,\tau \text{ a level automorphism attached to } \gamma^{-1} \text{ preserving the chart algebra},\ J' = \tau^{*}\bigl(\mathfrak{N}^{\,n}\bigr)\,\Bigr\},$$
--   where $\mathfrak{N}$ denotes the contraction along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t))$, $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0)$ and $\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$, and $\tau^{*}$ is the preimage under the restriction of $\tau$ to `chartAlgFin A K j`. Thus the same family of level automorphisms, indexed exactly as in `hJ`, computes every power of $J$, the power being taken on the local ideal $\mathfrak{N}$ before transport; for $n = 1$ the assertion is the hypothesis `hJ` itself.
--
--   This is the step which shows that the weighted centre $J$ of the supersingular blow-up chart, defined as the intersection of the translates of the local centre $\mathfrak{N}$ under the automorphisms of $K$ attached to $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, has all of its powers computed by the same orbit intersection with $\mathfrak{N}$ replaced by $\mathfrak{N}^n$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.mem_weightedCentre_pow_of_eq_pow_mul_mem_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.mem_weightedCentre_pow_of_eq_pow_mul_mem_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked) in the analysis of the integral model of the modular curve at a supersingular point.
